cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Occultations.jl, please cite it as below."
title: "Occultations.jl: reduction and modelling of stellar occultations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kretlow
    given-names: Mike
    email: mike@kretlow.de
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8858-3420"
    affiliation: "German Center for Astrophysics (DZA)"
    website: "https://github.com/mkretlow"
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mkretlow/Occultations.jl"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Julia package for the reduction and modelling of stellar occultations by small
  bodies: shadow tracks, light-curve timing with diffraction and stellar diameter,
  general limb fits (2-D ellipse, multi-event 3-D ellipsoid with rotational amplitude
  and phase constraints, shape meshes) with negative chords, ray-traced atmospheres,
  astrometry, uncertainties from covariances, likelihood profiles and MCMC, and maps.
keywords:
  - stellar occultations
  - trans-Neptunian objects
  - asteroids
  - astrometry
  - shape models
  - atmospheres
  - Julia
